# Byte-exact reproduction across platforms.
#
# Geometry exporters (STL/OBJ/3MF/JSON) and Go example `// Output:` blocks are
# compared byte-for-byte against committed golden files by tests that run on the
# Windows CI runner too. Git's autocrlf would rewrite LF-committed blobs to CRLF
# on checkout there, so a golden file would gain stray \r bytes and stop matching
# the library's LF output — a spurious CI failure on an otherwise-correct tree.
#
# `-text` disables ALL end-of-line conversion, so every checkout reproduces the
# committed blob EXACTLY on every platform.
* -text
